{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation saw.</b> In the Jerusalem Targum it explains that they saw Moses descending from the mountain, his garments torn and ashes on his head, weeping and saying: Woe for you, Aaron my brother. Another interpretation: we find the language of knowledge called seeing — ״וירא שר האופים״, ״וירא יעקב כי יש שבר״, ״ולבי ראה הרבה חכמה ודעת״, ״וראיתי אני בלבי״."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:56.027698807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}